        "locale": "quy",
        "key": "formats22_select_page",
        "english": "Choose a page",
        "proposed": "Huk rapita akllay",
        "decision": "accept",
        "final_value": "Huk rapita akllay",
        "rationale": "Huk is one/an individual page, appropriate to a chooser that selects exactly one page; rapi-ta marks that page as direct object, and aklla-y is a second-person singular imperative/command form. Object-before-verb ordering is natural. The whole title invites a choice, not a completed selection and not every page. Independent official same-variety indexed Rapi entry explicitly includes a notebook/book page as second sense, so the earlier botanical-leaf-only evidence limitation no longer applies to this basic noun. Unaspirated rapi and kichay conform to Ayacucho-Chanka; no Collao raphi or Bolivian laqhi substitution. Existing XML anchors only corroborate current consistency.",
        "confidence": "high for this bounded basic control; indexed-source access limitation retained",
