        "rationale": "Rapi-ta is the selected page as direct object; kicha-y is the open command. Absence of an article is normal, with definiteness supplied by the selected-page context. Digital opening is a modest contextual extension of opening/accessing, not an assertion that rendering has succeeded or all pages will load. Independent official same-variety indexed Rapi entry explicitly includes a notebook/book page as second sense, so the earlier botanical-leaf-only evidence limitation no longer applies to this basic noun. Unaspirated rapi and kichay conform to Ayacucho-Chanka; no Collao raphi or Bolivian laqhi substitution. Existing XML anchors only corroborate current consistency.",
